        : isSanJuanHub
        ? 'Choose one access section at a time when starting out. The upper Navajo Dam tailwater differs from the lower river’s diversion and fence hazards, and the Farmington city segments have posted public access rules. The longer trips remain in the picker with intermediate access notes; check the exact route and gauge before setting a shuttle.'
        : isTruckeeHub
        ? 'Start with one of the six documented sections below. The Floriston reach is technical whitewater; Reno–Sparks routes include urban access and whitewater-park features; the lower Truckee includes a required Derby Dam portage and a tribal permit for the Wadsworth take-out. The other 18 endpoint combinations remain available in the picker with their own route notes.'
        : `Compare current scores where available, along with water level, recent trend, weather, access, and route difficulty. Planning-only cards provide trip information without a live paddling recommendation.`
